      "content": "That mood is perfect. I really want to lean into that \"suffocating\" feeling through the actual spoken words. To make it authentic to the 1940s South, the way the sheriff speaks to him shouldn't just be threatening, it should be degrading. In that era, law enforcement didn't treat Black men like equals even if they were respected in their own communities. Can you write out a few lines of actual dialogue where the sheriff uses the kind of derogatory language or slurs that were common back then? It's important for the grit and the historical accuracy of the tension.",
